<title>EGYPT: Egypt crude output, natgas fall in December-EGPC.</title>
<headline>Egypt crude output, natgas fall in December-EGPC.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian crude oil production fell in December to an average of 832,000 barrels per day (bpd) from 835,000 bpd in November, the state's Egyptian General Petroleum Corp (EGPC) said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Natural gas output fell slightly to 1.11 billion cubic feet per day from 1.31 billion cubic feet in November.</p>
<p>Condensate production rose to 35,800 bpd from 35,700 bpd, while propane and butane output was unchanged at 31,600 bpd, EGPC said.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
